1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"2f5576655005386419a0a30c29e91b48bf04d13cf11c0c9e12d2bcbd9927d5c8","event_uuid":"020fddef-ab82-4b95-83a5-03f07dc93584","position":{"commit_sha":"f78e066646c80ab47a82ab4004ba2617647a061e","position":"1788617861268935001-020fddef-ab82-4b95-83a5-03f07dc93584"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788617171374165001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"80601f89-4bfe-47b2-8f4c-bbb3c36a87a1","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"0165-f432-0580-4117"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n`infra/scripts/container-cap.sh` was added after the original comment-remediation inventory and contains repeated incident history, duplicated mechanism explanations, and obvious narration. Audit basis is `origin/main@0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e`.\n\n## Approach\nCondense only ordinary shell-comment blocks identified by stable code anchors. Preserve shell behavior, embedded programs, rendered unit-file text, operator-facing diagnostics, and directives byte-for-byte.\n\nThe content guard compares immutable before/final blobs after removing only the explicit allowlisted shell-comment spans from each. It rejects changes outside those spans. It separately preserves the shebang and SC2086 directive with their next executable statements. Every heredoc body remains exact: comments inside the rendered systemd units and embedded Python are runtime content, not editable shell comments.\n\n## Scope\n- File header before `set -uo pipefail` — retain the shared writable-layer budget, XFS `pquota`/reboot constraint, per-container/create-time limitation, reaper limits, three protected sets, bounded-debris formula, and side-effect-free mode contract; remove outage chronology and repeated emphasis.\n- Share/policy declarations through `REAPER_UNIT` — retain single sourcing from `docker-storage-cap.sh`, no guessed fallback, grace window, label/name/running protections, quota filesystem, nested timer/unit bounds, and Docker-call bound.\n- Validation and `_docker` blocks — retain fail-loud numeric validation and the no-`timeout` degradation.\n- Shell prose around `render_*`, `write_units`, `reaper_in_effect`, and `quota_enforced` — retain exact rendered-unit ownership, timer/content checks, and fail-closed quota enforcement. Do not change heredoc bytes.\n- Shell prose around `census_format`, `census`, and `protected` — retain one `SizeRw` census, dynamically derived label columns, absent-label normalization, and independent protections.\n- Shell prose inside `reap` — retain unreadable-share/census refusal, six-field `read`, running/protected/grace handling, oldest-first target, no-force/no-volume removal, and loud residual-over-budget limits.\n- Shell prose before `finished_epoch` — retain portable Python parsing and never-started timestamp semantics. Preserve the entire embedded Python heredoc exactly.\n- `report_state`, argument handling, `--print-env`, and install prose — retain strongest-supported regime reporting, single-quoted eval-safe values, installed-copy fallback, timer enablement, and final status.\n\nConsumers include `compose-up.sh`, `observability.sh`, `docker-storage-cap.sh`, the operations runbook, Terraform alarm guidance, and the container-cap/storage/observability tests.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Only allowlisted ordinary shell-comment spans or adjacent blank lines change.\n- [ ] Executable shell lines remain byte-identical.\n- [ ] All heredoc bodies and operator-facing output strings remain byte-identical.\n- [ ] The shebang and SC2086 directive retain exact text and placement.\n- [ ] Every edited block is shorter and removes repetition, chronology, ornament, or obvious narration.\n- [ ] A non-author reviewer posts one leaf-linked TSV row per edited block with immutable before/final citations, preserved contract/consumer, before/after words, and both verdicts.\n- [ ] Every TSV row records `semantic-preservation=PASS` and `bloat-removal=PASS`; missing or failing rows block closure.\n- [ ] Focused tests, ShellCheck policy, path-scoped `git diff --check`, and worktree-venv `make verify` pass.\n\n## Verification\nRun the recorded allowlist/executable/heredoc/directive comparator; `tests/scripts/test_container_cap.py`, `tests/scripts/test_observability_container_layers.py`, and `tests/scripts/test_docker_storage_cap.py`; `scripts/check_shellcheck.py`; path-scoped `git diff --check`; and `make verify`. The independent TSV is authoritative for prose quality.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/scripts/container-cap.sh","reason":"Condense allowlisted shell comments while preserving executable, heredoc, directive, and operator-output contracts."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","49ac-d7e5-f383-4d7f"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"49ac-d7e5-f383-4d7f","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["comment-remediation","comments","infra"],"ticket_id":"7beb-8c21-63f4-4760","ticket_type":"task","title":"Condense comments in infra/scripts/container-cap.sh","verify_commands":[{"command":"rtk proxy env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest -q tests/scripts/test_container_cap.py tests/scripts/test_observability_container_layers.py tests/scripts/test_docker_storage_cap.py","dd_id":"focused","dd_text":"Container-cap, storage-budget, and observability integration contracts pass."},{"command":"rtk proxy env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_shellcheck.py","dd_id":"shellcheck","dd_text":"Shell syntax and ShellCheck policy pass."},{"command":"rtk git diff --check HEAD^ HEAD -- infra/scripts/container-cap.sh","dd_id":"diff","dd_text":"The impacted shell path contains no whitespace errors."},{"command":"rtk proxy env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify","dd_id":"full","dd_text":"The repository verification gate passes."}]},"source_event_uuids":["cbabff09-d57b-49d3-949e-625749e89d6e","7a94531c-158b-488f-96c2-e3f183b567b1","08ec4f97-a4ed-4c47-a844-2502e9edb854","80601f89-4bfe-47b2-8f4c-bbb3c36a87a1","020fddef-ab82-4b95-83a5-03f07dc93584"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788623680955837001,"uuid":"9b7455bb-7864-44d4-b37d-a2dce87934ea"}